<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>HTML Text Formatting Demonstration</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Essential HTML Text Formatting</h1>
    
    <p>This paragraph demonstrates how to use <b>bold text</b> to visually draw attention to specific words.</p>
    
    <p>This paragraph demonstrates how to use <i>italic text</i> to denote a title, term, or alternative voice.</p>
    
    <p>This paragraph demonstrates how to use <u>underlined text</u>, which is helpful for emphasizing specific spelling errors or book titles.</p>
    
    <p>This paragraph demonstrates how to use <sup>superscript text</sup>, which is commonly used for math exponents like E = mc<sup>2</sup> or footnotes<sup>[1]</sup>.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>Combined Text Formatting Examples</h2>
    <p>You can also nest tags to create <b><i>bold and italic text</i></b> or even <b><u><i>bold, underlined, and italic text</i></u></b> together.</p>

</body>
</html>
